    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d223">

                <pb facs="0364" n="270" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg270"/>

                <head>No. 223.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Señor Perez</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-10-07"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 7,
                        1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 3d instant, saying that the Nicaraguan Congress had rejected
                    the treaty of July 26, 1887, for the adjustment of the boundary difficulty
                    between that Government and Costa Rica, and to observe that I thus learn with
                    regret that the expected course of direct settlement of the questions between
                    two countries to which the United States are equally friendly is
                    interrupted.</p>
                <p>Accept sir, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
